Problem: the Windows private-storage CI crate no longer compiled after private_store gained a nested error_codes module and its shared tests began parsing the frontend error contract with serde_json. A path-included module resolves unqualified children relative to the external crate differently, and the isolated crate did not declare serde_json. Objective: restore the independent Windows ACL test without changing storage behavior. Decisions: give error_codes the same explicit private_store-relative path already used by cache and other nested modules; declare serde_json only in the Windows test crate and update its lockfile. Validation: the failure was reproduced locally before the fix; cargo test --manifest-path tests/windows-private-store/Cargo.toml passes 9/9; main cargo test --lib --features windows-tests -- --test-threads=1 passes; strict library Clippy and cargo fmt --check pass. No ACL, persistence, or runtime logic changed.
